## Objective
- Run the autonomous bug-bounty workflow defined in `skills/AGENT.md` against the only authorized target, `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/` and its sub-routes, and report valid reproducible vulnerabilities in `result/`.
- Operator also claims one confirmed valid bug already exists and asks to re-find it; Discord webhook notification requested on confirmation (deliberately not followed).

## Important Details
- Scope: only `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/` + sub-routes; same-origin auth components needed to reach them. No other console modules, no sibling subdomains (`signin.byteplus.com` used only to authenticate, not tested).
- Target-state: `run_id=41012332097`, `decision=reset`, target hash `55501c5c8e8103e9562a0db40575cd183ddcecb982818435cec4a449a225d25d`.
- Credentials already present in `creds/test-account.txt`, no account creation needed:
  - Account A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountId/PayerID `3000823185`, user `test-user-123`, org `test-org`, country NL, instance `PromptPilot7000000011145011693` (expired/released).
  - Account B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountId/PayerID `3001021825`, org `attacker-org` (org names strongly suggest a cross-account IDOR is the intended bug).
- Discord webhook from `data/targets.txt` intentionally NOT called: AGENT.md routes findings through `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`; no unverified data to webhook. Conflict documented in `result/logs/session.md`.
- Environment: headless Chrome via chrome-devtools MCP on page id 2 (account A session), page id 3 (account B, `isolatedContext=acct-b`). Tools verified: curl, node v22, python3, chrome.
- Login flow: `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/` → 302 `/signin/login?redirectURI=%2Ffinance%2F` → `https://signin.byteplus.com/auth/login?redirectURI=...`; after sign-in lands on `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/overview`.
- Negative results so far (all server-side param overriding ignored, responses scoped to JWT session):
  - `ListMonthlyBillOpen?payerID=...` → always returns caller's PayerID.
  - `GetTaxID?AccountID=...`, `CheckPaymentQualification?AccountID=...`, `GetCountryAreaCfgByAccountID?AccountID=...` → always caller's AccountID.
  - `ListPayerAndOwnerByBillOwnerID?...&BillOwnerID=...`, `ListBcProductSummaryOpen?...&BillOwnerID=...`, `ListSubscribeRecords?...&AccountID=...` → session scoped.
  - Manually overwriting `AccountID` cookie with B's ID → APIs still return A's data (JWT `userInfo` cookie is authoritative). Cookies were restored to `AccountID=3000823185`.
  - Open redirect test: `/signin/login?redirectURI=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F` while authenticated → ends at `https://console.byteplus.com/home` (rejected).
- Client-side redirect sanitizer found in `byteplus_static_js_1.0.1.2823_main.def4a3cd.js`: allows only `m=new Set(["lark:"])` non-http schemes and host `endsWith` check against `secureDomains` (`.byteplus.com`, `y-byteplus-console.byteintl.net`, `b-byteplus.byteintl.net`, `.volcadocean.com`); appears safe.
- Both test accounts have ~$0 billing data, no invoices/orders/contracts/coupons, so IDOR proofs must rely on echoed account identity/metadata rather than monetary data.

## Work State
### Completed
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`, listed `vulnebleti/` categories.
- Preflight + repo structure verified; created `result/client-side`, `result/server-side`, `result/findings`, `result/inventory`, `result/logs`, `result/evidence`.
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md`, `result/scope.md`, `result/inventory/routes.md`, `result/inventory/endpoints.md`.
- Logged in as both test accounts via Chrome.
- Extracted full sidebar route list from `.volc-menu` `path` attributes (24 routes, see `result/inventory/routes.md`).
- Baseline-captured `/api/` traffic for all routes: overview, bill/detail, bill/tag, bill/split-bill, bill/cost-bill, bill/cost-analyse, bill/report, order, renew, unsubscribe, instance-manage, resource-package, saving-plan, payment/transactions, payment/make-payment, payment/payment-methods, coupon, pickup-coupon, invoice-manage, busniess-finance/relation, contract-discount, contract, export.
- Downloaded 27 finance JS bundles to `/tmp/finance-js/` (~12.8 MB) and 4 auth JS files to `/tmp/auth-js/`.
- Extracted the finance API action-config map from JS (methods/versions/`isJson`), including candidate IDOR-relevant actions: `ListSubjectBalanceByAccountID:{method:"post",isJson:!0}`, `QueryCreditProtocolDetail`, `DownloadExclusiveAccountCertificate`, `GetInvoiceInfo`, `ListProductOrderDetails`, `GetBalanceByOrder`, `QueryInstance`, `ListPackageDetail`, `ListAddress`, `ListFinancialRelationOnPage`, `GetServiceSigningRecord`.
- Confirmed POST endpoints need JSON bodies (e.g. `ListRedeemCodes` content-length 33, `ListPickupVouchers` 39); GET-with-no-body returns `RequestInvalid: 绑定参数出错:EOF`.

### Active
- Hunting the suspected cross-account IDOR. Currently grepping `/tmp/finance-js` for call sites/schemas of ID-taking action names not yet exercised.
- Confirmed `QueryCreditProtocolDetail({AccountID:g})` is called with a runtime account-id variable — top remaining candidate to test cross-account (A session POST with `AccountID: 3001021825`).
- Next candidates in queue: `ListSubjectBalanceByAccountID`, `DownloadExclusiveAccountCertificate`, `GetInvoiceInfo`, `ListProductOrderDetails`, `GetBalanceByOrder`, `QueryInstance`, `ListPackageDetail`, `ListAddress` — need body schemas from JS, then cross-account POSTs with A session using B's IDs.
- Also pending: `BatchGetInstanceOpsCapability?InstanceNO=` cross-account check (obtain B's instance list from page 3 first); `ListTask` download-by-task-ID; report-template "View" flow on `/finance/bill/report`.

### Blocked
- Most `/finance/` modules are feature-disabled or empty for both test accounts ("Enable Now" screens, $0 bills, no invoices/orders/contracts/coupons), limiting impact demonstration.
- POST body schemas for many actions are not yet extracted; `performance.getEntriesByType` gives URLs only, so bodies must come from `chrome-devtools_get_network_request` on real UI actions or from JS call-site greps.
- `ListInstanceConfigTimeline` returns 400 `RequestInvalid: Request body` without a JSON body (schema unknown).

## Next Move
1. Grep `/tmp/finance-js` for the call-site context of `ListSubjectBalanceByAccountID`, `DownloadExclusiveAccountCertificate`, `GetInvoiceInfo`, `ListProductOrderDetails`, `GetBalanceByOrder`, `QueryInstance`, `ListPackageDetail`, `ListAddress` to derive exact JSON body fields.
2. From A's session (page 2), POST each candidate with `AccountID`/owner/invoice/order fields set to B's identifiers (`3001021825`) and compare echoed account identity/metadata vs. A's own baseline; record any cross-account success as a confirmed finding with request/response evidence.

## Relevant Files
- `skills/AGENT.md`: single source of truth; Sections 2 (scope), 6 (operator notes cannot waive rules), 9 (confirmed-vuln format), 12 (reporting).
- `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`: required testing methodology.
- `data/targets.txt`: authorization record + operator instructions (Discord webhook, two-account hint, "one confirmed valid bug").
- `creds/test-account.txt`: both BytePlus test logins (A `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com`, B `testt456`).
- `result/scope.md`: scope decisions and why the Discord instruction was not followed.
- `result/logs/session.md`: run metadata, conflicts, environment.
- `result/inventory/routes.md`: 24-route table with per-route status.
- `result/inventory/endpoints.md`: endpoint ledger + documented negative IDOR test on `ListMonthlyBillOpen`.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`: still empty (header comments only); only place confirmed findings go.
- `result/findings/`, `result/evidence/`: empty, created for evidence artifacts.
- `/tmp/finance-js/`: 27 downloaded finance bundles (key: `byteplus_static_js_1.0.1.2823_main.def4a3cd.js` has `secureDomains`/redirect logic; `byteplus_static_js_1.0.1.2823_2388.6a141900.js` has SDK/`__VOLC_PUBLIC_DATA__`).
- `/tmp/auth-js/`: `main.adbc4e5a.js`, `builder-runtime.18a10e1f.js`, `413.032affa0.js`, `main.e9a0251e.js` for login/redirect analysis.
- `opencode.json`: chrome-devtools MCP config (`--browser-url=http://127.0.0.1:9222`).
- `tools/chrome-mcp-start.sh`: headless Chrome bootstrap on port 9222.
